IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: ss 368 to 371 -- what a foreign company lodges to be registered,
-- the duties of its directors and authorised representatives to give it information, the saving provisions for particulars
-- lodged before 3 January 2016, the refusal of registration, the registered office and the authorised representatives,
-- the transitional rule on contact addresses, and the notice and certificate the Registrar issues. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind,
-- with the words); NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind, with the reason). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A time limit is counted only with sg-periods.l4. Where the text says "within N days after X" of a duty, an act on the day of X itself
-- is taken to be in time (fork F-P1 in NOTES.md): the function used is `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after`.

§ `Section 368(1): what a foreign company must lodge before it establishes a place of business`

-- One field per paragraph of s 368(1). The paragraphs that apply only on a condition carry the condition as a field of its own.
DECLARE `s 368(1) lodgment` HAS
    `s 368(1)(a) it has lodged the name of the foreign company and the address of its registered office in its place of incorporation or formation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(b) it has lodged a certified copy of the certificate of its incorporation or registration in its place of incorporation or formation, or a document of similar effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(c) the law relating to incorporation, formation or registration in its place of incorporation, formation or original registration requires its charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument to be registered or lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(c) it has lodged a certified copy of its charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(d) it has lodged a list of its directors with the particulars the register of directors of a company incorporated under this Act must contain and, for each director, his or her residential address and contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(e) it has lodged a notice stating the names, nationalities and other identification particulars of one or more natural persons resident in Singapore appointed as its authorised representatives and authorised to accept service of process and notices, with each one's residential address and contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(f) it has lodged the statement in the prescribed form confirming that each authorised representative has consented to act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(g) it has lodged notice of the situation of its registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(g) the registered office is open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours on each business day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(g) it has lodged notice of the days and hours during which the registered office is open and accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(h)(i) it has lodged the notice in the prescribed form giving the identification number or registration number on the corporate entity register (if applicable), or other similar evidence of identity acceptable to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(h)(ii) the notice in the prescribed form describes the business carried on by the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(h)(iii) the notice in the prescribed form gives the type of legal form or legal entity of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(i) the law for the time being applicable to the foreign company in the place of its incorporation or formation requires audited financial statements of its head office to be prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 368(1)(i) it has lodged a copy of the latest audited financial statements of its head office` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The paragraphs, one by one, that the lodgment does not yet satisfy. A paragraph with its own condition is satisfied where the condition is absent.
GIVEN complied IS A BOOLEAN
      label IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` MEANS
    IF complied THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST label

GIVEN lodged IS A `s 368(1) lodgment`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` MEANS
    concat (LIST (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(a) it has lodged the name of the foreign company and the address of its registered office in its place of incorporation or formation`) "(a) the name and registered-office address in the place of incorporation"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(b) it has lodged a certified copy of the certificate of its incorporation or registration in its place of incorporation or formation, or a document of similar effect`) "(b) a certified copy of the certificate of incorporation or registration"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` ((NOT lodged's `s 368(1)(c) the law relating to incorporation, formation or registration in its place of incorporation, formation or original registration requires its charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument to be registered or lodged`) OR lodged's `s 368(1)(c) it has lodged a certified copy of its charter, statute, constitution or memorandum or articles or other instrument constituting or defining its constitution`) "(c) a certified copy of the charter, statute, constitution or articles"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(d) it has lodged a list of its directors with the particulars the register of directors of a company incorporated under this Act must contain and, for each director, his or her residential address and contact address`) "(d) the list of directors"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(e) it has lodged a notice stating the names, nationalities and other identification particulars of one or more natural persons resident in Singapore appointed as its authorised representatives and authorised to accept service of process and notices, with each one's residential address and contact address`) "(e) the notice of the authorised representatives"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(f) it has lodged the statement in the prescribed form confirming that each authorised representative has consented to act`) "(f) the consent statement"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(g) it has lodged notice of the situation of its registered office in Singapore`) "(g) notice of the situation of the registered office in Singapore"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(g) the registered office is open and accessible to the public during ordinary business hours on each business day` OR lodged's `s 368(1)(g) it has lodged notice of the days and hours during which the registered office is open and accessible to the public`) "(g) notice of the days and hours the registered office is open"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(h)(i) it has lodged the notice in the prescribed form giving the identification number or registration number on the corporate entity register (if applicable), or other similar evidence of identity acceptable to the Registrar`) "(h)(i) the identification number or registration number"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(h)(ii) the notice in the prescribed form describes the business carried on by the foreign company`) "(h)(ii) the description of the business"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` (lodged's `s 368(1)(h)(iii) the notice in the prescribed form gives the type of legal form or legal entity of the foreign company`) "(h)(iii) the type of legal form or legal entity"), (`s 368(1) the paragraph if not complied with` ((NOT lodged's `s 368(1)(i) the law for the time being applicable to the foreign company in the place of its incorporation or formation requires audited financial statements of its head office to be prepared`) OR lodged's `s 368(1)(i) it has lodged a copy of the latest audited financial statements of its head office`) "(i) a copy of the latest audited financial statements of the head office"))

-- src:23713 | Documents, etc., to be lodged by foreign companies having
-- src:23714 | place of business in Singapore
-- src:23716 | 368.—(1) Every foreign company must, before it establishes a
-- src:23717 | place of business or commences to carry on business in Singapore,
-- src:23718 | lodge with the Registrar for registration —
-- src:23723 | (a) the name of the foreign company and the address of the
-- src:23724 | registered office of the company in its place of
-- src:23725 | incorporation or formation;
-- src:23727 | (b) a certified copy of the certificate of its incorporation or
-- src:23728 | registration in its place of incorporation or formation or a
-- src:23729 | document of similar effect;
-- src:23731 | (c) a certified copy of its charter, statute, constitution or
-- src:23732 | memorandum or articles or other instrument constituting
-- src:23733 | or defining its constitution but only if such document is
-- src:23734 | required to be registered or lodged under the law relating to
-- src:23735 | the incorporation, formation or registration of the foreign
-- src:23736 | company in its place of incorporation, formation or
-- src:23737 | original registration;
-- src:23739 | (d) a list of its directors containing similar particulars with
-- src:23740 | respect to its directors as are by this Act required to be
-- src:23741 | contained in the register of directors of a company
-- src:23742 | incorporated under this Act and, in respect of each
-- src:23743 | director, his or her residential address and contact address;
-- src:23747 | (e) a notice stating the names, nationalities and other
-- src:23748 | identification particulars of one or more natural persons
-- src:23749 | resident in Singapore who are appointed as the company’s
-- src:23750 | authorised representatives and authorised as such to accept
-- src:23751 | on its behalf service of process and any notice required to
-- src:23752 | be served on the company, and in respect of each
-- src:23753 | authorised representative, his or her residential address
-- src:23754 | and contact address;
-- src:23758 | (f) a statement by or on behalf of the foreign company in the
-- src:23759 | prescribed form confirming that each of its authorised
-- src:23760 | representatives referred to in the notice lodged under
-- src:23761 | paragraph (e) has consented to act as such (called in this
-- src:23762 | section and section 370 the consent statement);
-- src:23764 | (g) notice of the situation of its registered office in Singapore
-- src:23765 | and, unless the office is open and accessible to the public
-- src:23766 | during ordinary business hours on each business day, the
-- src:23771 | days and hours during which it is open and accessible to the
-- src:23772 | public;
-- src:23774 | (h) a notice in the prescribed form containing the following
-- src:23775 | particulars:
-- src:23777 | (i) the identification number or registration number of
-- src:23778 | the foreign company on the corporate entity register
-- src:23779 | (if applicable) of the jurisdiction where the foreign
-- src:23780 | company is formed or incorporated or any other
-- src:23781 | similar evidence of identity acceptable to the
-- src:23782 | Registrar;
-- src:23786 | (ii) a description of the business carried on by the foreign
-- src:23787 | company; and
-- src:23789 | (iii) the type of legal form or legal entity of the foreign
-- src:23790 | company; and
-- src:23792 | (i) where the law for the time being applicable to the foreign
-- src:23793 | company in the place of its incorporation or formation
-- src:23794 | requires audited financial statements of its head office to be
-- src:23795 | prepared, a copy of the latest audited financial statements
-- src:23796 | of its head office,
-- src:23798 | and on payment of the appropriate fees and subject to this Act, the
-- src:23799 | Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division by
-- src:23800 | registration of the documents.
@ref s 368(1) (src:23713-23800)
GIVEN lodged IS A `s 368(1) lodgment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` lodged EQUALS EMPTY
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every foreign company must, before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business in Singapore, lodge with the Registrar for registration — (a) ... (i) ..." (a duty not met: the provision's own question; paragraph (c) is required "but only if" the law of the place of incorporation requires the instrument to be registered or lodged, and paragraph (i) only "where" that law requires audited financial statements of the head office)

-- "before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business in Singapore": the day the documents were lodged is before the day it began.
@ref s 368(1) (src:23716-23718)
GIVEN `the day the documents were lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day the foreign company established a place of business or commenced to carry on business in Singapore` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(1) the foreign company lodged the documents before it began` MEANS
    IF `the day the documents were lodged` LESS THAN `the day the foreign company established a place of business or commenced to carry on business in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business in Singapore, lodge" (a lodgment on or after the day it began is not before it)

-- "and on payment of the appropriate fees and subject to this Act, the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division".
@ref s 368(1) (src:23798-23800)
GIVEN `the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appropriate fees have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this Act, such as section 369 or section 378, requires or permits the Registrar to refuse the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(1) the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` AND `the appropriate fees have been paid`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and on payment of the appropriate fees ..., the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division by registration of the documents" (the duty arises on the lodgment and on payment; a duty whose "on payment" gate is unmet: fork F-D1)
    ELSE (IF `a provision of this Act, such as section 369 or section 378, requires or permits the Registrar to refuse the registration`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to this Act" makes the duty yield to the provisions of this Act that bear on registration, which are other sections
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 368(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 368(1) lodge with the Registrar for registration the documents the subsection lists`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the party is the foreign company, the act is the lodgment, the time limit is "before" it begins.
-- WITHIN counts days from the day the trace starts: the number given is the last day on which a lodgment is still before the day the company begins.
@ref s 368(1) (src:23716-23718)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the last day, counted in days from now, on which lodging is still before the foreign company establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 368(1) act`
`s 368(1) the foreign company must lodge the documents before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 368(1) lodge with the Registrar for registration the documents the subsection lists`
    WITHIN `the last day, counted in days from now, on which lodging is still before the foreign company establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the documents were not lodged before the foreign company established a place of business or commenced to carry on business in Singapore"

§ `Section 368(2) to (4): service on a director or authorised representative, inspection, the 1967 transition`

-- src:23804 | (2) Any document required to be served under this Act on a director
-- src:23805 | or an authorised representative of a foreign company is sufficiently
-- src:23806 | served if addressed to the director or authorised representative and
-- src:23807 | left at or sent by post to his or her residential address or contact
-- src:23808 | address.
@ref s 368(2) (src:23804-23808)
GIVEN `the document is required to be served under this Act on a director or an authorised representative of a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is addressed to the director or authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the contact address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is required to be served under this Act on a director or an authorised representative of a foreign company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any document required to be served under this Act on a director or an authorised representative of a foreign company": a document not required to be so served is outside the subsection
    ELSE (IF `the document is addressed to the director or authorised representative` AND (`the document is left at, or sent by post to, the residential address` OR `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the contact address`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficiently served if addressed to the director or authorised representative and left at or sent by post to his or her residential address or contact address" (a condition the text introduces with "if": marginal reading (a); the other reading is NOTHING, since other ways of serving are not excluded)

-- src:23814 | (3) The following must be made available for inspection at the
-- src:23815 | registered office of the foreign company during the hours in which the
-- src:23816 | registered office of the company is accessible to the public:
-- src:23821 | (a) a copy of the memorandum of appointment or power of
-- src:23822 | attorney appointing each authorised representative of the
-- src:23823 | company in such manner as to be binding on the company;
-- src:23825 | (b) where the memorandum of appointment or power of
-- src:23826 | attorney mentioned in paragraph (a) is executed by a
-- src:23827 | person on behalf of the company, a copy of the deed or
-- src:23828 | document by which that person is authorised to execute the
-- src:23829 | memorandum of appointment or power of attorney,
-- src:23830 | verified by statutory declaration in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 368(3) (src:23814-23830)
GIVEN `the copy of the memorandum of appointment or power of attorney appointing each authorised representative is available for inspection at the registered office during the hours it is accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum of appointment or power of attorney was executed by a person on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the deed or document by which that person is authorised to execute it, verified by statutory declaration in the prescribed manner, is available for inspection at the registered office during the hours it is accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(3) what the subsection requires to be available for inspection is available` MEANS
    IF `the copy of the memorandum of appointment or power of attorney appointing each authorised representative is available for inspection at the registered office during the hours it is accessible to the public`
       AND ((NOT `the memorandum of appointment or power of attorney was executed by a person on behalf of the company`) OR `a copy of the deed or document by which that person is authorised to execute it, verified by statutory declaration in the prescribed manner, is available for inspection at the registered office during the hours it is accessible to the public`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following must be made available for inspection at the registered office of the foreign company during the hours in which the registered office of the company is accessible to the public: (a) a copy of the memorandum of appointment or power of attorney ...; (b) where the memorandum ... is executed by a person on behalf of the company, a copy of the deed or document by which that person is authorised ..." (a duty not met; the text names no bearer, so no regulative rule is derived: fork F-B1)

-- src:23834 | (4) Subsection (1) applies to a foreign company which was not
-- src:23835 | registered under the repealed written laws but which, immediately
-- src:23836 | before 29 December 1967, had a place of business or was carrying on
-- src:23837 | business in Singapore and, on that date, had a place of business or was
-- src:23838 | carrying on business in Singapore, as if it established that place of
-- src:23839 | business or commenced to carry on that business on that date.
@ref s 368(4) (src:23834-23839)
GIVEN `the foreign company was not registered under the repealed written laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before 29 December 1967 the foreign company had a place of business or was carrying on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 29 December 1967 the foreign company had a place of business or was carrying on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(4) subsection (1) applies to the foreign company as if it began on 29 December 1967` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company was not registered under the repealed written laws` AND `immediately before 29 December 1967 the foreign company had a place of business or was carrying on business in Singapore` AND `on 29 December 1967 the foreign company had a place of business or was carrying on business in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) applies to a foreign company which was not registered under the repealed written laws but which, immediately before 29 December 1967, had a place of business or was carrying on business in Singapore and, on that date, had ..." names the companies it reaches, without "only"

§ `Section 368A: the duty of directors and authorised representatives to give the foreign company information`

DECLARE `s 368A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs`

-- The penalty of s 368A(5): the offence, the fine, the term (none stated) and the default penalty.
DECLARE `s 368A(5) penalty` HAS
    `s 368A(5) the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 368A(5) the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 368A(5) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 368A(5) a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:23843 | Duty of directors and authorised representatives to provide
-- src:23844 | information to foreign company
-- src:23846 | 368A.—(1) A director must give the foreign company any
-- src:23847 | information the company needs to comply with section 372(1) as
-- src:23848 | soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after his or her initial
-- src:23849 | appointment, unless he or she has previously given the information to
-- src:23850 | the company in writing.
@ref s 368A(1) (src:23843-23850)
GIVEN `the director has previously given the information to the foreign company in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(1) the director must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 372(1)` MEANS
    IF `the director has previously given the information to the foreign company in writing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she has previously given the information to the company in writing"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 368A(1) (src:23846-23850)
GIVEN `the day of the director's initial appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day the director gave the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the director's initial appointment` `the day the director gave the information` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after his or her initial appointment" (a period the text fixes in its own words; the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

@ref s 368A(1) (src:23846-23850)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 368A act`
`s 368A(1) a director must give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment"

-- src:23854 | (2) An authorised representative must give the foreign company —
-- src:23856 | (a) any information the company needs to comply with
-- src:23857 | section 370(4) as soon as practicable but not later than
-- src:23858 | 14 days after his or her initial appointment, unless he or she
-- src:23859 | has previously given the information to the company in
-- src:23860 | writing; and
-- src:23862 | (b) any information the company needs to comply with
-- src:23863 | section 372(1) as soon as practicable but not later than
-- src:23864 | 14 days after any change in his or her particulars.
@ref s 368A(2) (src:23854-23864)
GIVEN `the authorised representative has previously given the information to the foreign company in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 370(4)` MEANS
    IF `the authorised representative has previously given the information to the foreign company in writing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she has previously given the information to the company in writing"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 368A(2) (src:23856-23860)
GIVEN `the day of the authorised representative's initial appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day the authorised representative gave the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the authorised representative's initial appointment` `the day the authorised representative gave the information` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after his or her initial appointment" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 368A(2) (src:23862-23864)
GIVEN `the day his or her particulars changed` IS A DATE
      `the day the authorised representative gave the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(2)(b) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the change in his or her particulars` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day his or her particulars changed` `the day the authorised representative gave the information` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after any change in his or her particulars" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 368A(2) (src:23854-23860)
GIVEN `the name of the authorised representative` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 368A act`
`s 368A(2) an authorised representative must give the foreign company the information within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative`
    MUST `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` `the name of the authorised representative` BECAUSE "the authorised representative did not give the foreign company the information within 14 days"

-- src:23871 | (3) Despite subsection (1) or (2), a director or an authorised
-- src:23872 | representative must, subject to subsection (4), if requested by the
-- src:23873 | foreign company, give the company any information referred to in
-- src:23874 | section 368(1)(d) or (e) for the purpose of enabling the company to
-- src:23875 | confirm its record of such information or reinstate its record of the
-- src:23876 | information where the original record of the information has been
-- src:23877 | destroyed or lost.
@ref s 368A(3) (src:23871-23877)
GIVEN `the foreign company has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is information referred to in section 368(1)(d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to enable the company to confirm its record of the information or to reinstate it where the original record has been destroyed or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(3) the director or authorised representative must give the foreign company the information on request` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has requested the information` AND `the information is information referred to in section 368(1)(d) or (e)` AND `the purpose is to enable the company to confirm its record of the information or to reinstate it where the original record has been destroyed or lost`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director or an authorised representative must, subject to subsection (4), if requested by the foreign company, give the company any information referred to in section 368(1)(d) or (e) for the purpose of enabling the company to confirm its record ... or reinstate its record" (a duty whose "if requested" is unmet: fork F-D1)

-- src:23881 | (4) The director or authorised representative mentioned in
-- src:23882 | subsection (3) must furnish the information to the foreign company
-- src:23883 | as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after receipt of a
-- src:23884 | written request for such information from the company.
@ref s 368A(4) (src:23881-23884)
GIVEN `the day the director or authorised representative received the written request` IS A DATE
      `the day the director or authorised representative furnished the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368A(4) the information was furnished not later than 14 days after receipt of the written request` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the director or authorised representative received the written request` `the day the director or authorised representative furnished the information` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must furnish the information to the foreign company as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after receipt of a written request" (a period the text fixes in its own words)

@ref s 368A(4) (src:23881-23884)
GIVEN `the party who must furnish the information` IS A `s 365 party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 368A act`
`s 368A(4) the director or authorised representative must furnish the information within 14 days after the written request` MEANS
    PARTY `the party who must furnish the information`
    MUST `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the party who must furnish the information` BECAUSE "the information was not furnished within 14 days after receipt of the written request"

-- src:23888 | (5) A director or an authorised representative who is bound to
-- src:23889 | comply with a requirement under this section and fails to do so shall
-- src:23890 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:23891 | exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 368A(5) (src:23888-23891)
GIVEN `the person is bound to comply with a requirement under section 368A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 368A(5) penalty`
`s 368A(5) the penalty for a director or authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the person is bound to comply with a requirement under section 368A` AND `the person fails to comply with the requirement`
    THEN `s 368A(5) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 5000, NOTHING, JUST TRUE   -- "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty"; the subsection states no term of imprisonment (NOTHING-kind (silent)); the default penalty is s 408's
    ELSE `s 368A(5) penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director or an authorised representative who is bound to comply with a requirement under this section and fails to do so shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)

@ref s 368A(5) (src:23888-23891)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `the person is bound to comply with a requirement under section 368A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 368A(5) penalty`
`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 368A(5) the penalty for a director or authorised representative` `the person is bound to comply with a requirement under section 368A` `the person fails to comply with the requirement`
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 368A(5) the penalty for a director or authorised representative` `the person is bound to comply with a requirement under section 368A` `the person fails to comply with the requirement`
    OTHERWISE `s 368A(5) penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director or an authorised representative who is bound to comply with a requirement under this section" names the persons it reaches, without "only"

§ `Section 368B: particulars lodged before 3 January 2016`

-- src:23895 | Saving and transitional provisions for existing particulars of
-- src:23896 | directors and authorised representatives before 3 January
-- src:23897 | 2016
-- src:23899 | 368B.—(1) If a foreign company, whether incorporated before, on
-- src:23900 | or after 3 January 2016 —
-- src:23902 | (a) has lodged the name and particulars of one or more
-- src:23903 | directors with the Registrar as a director or directors (as the
-- src:23904 | case may be) of the foreign company under
-- src:23905 | section 368(1)(c) in force immediately prior to that date,
-- src:23906 | the name and particulars of the director or directors (as the
-- src:23907 | case may be) are to be treated as the name and particulars
-- src:23908 | of the company’s director or directors (as the case may be)
-- src:23909 | until a notification of any change to the information is
-- src:23910 | received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca); or
@ref s 368B(1)(a) (src:23895-23910)
GIVEN `the foreign company lodged the name and particulars of one or more directors under section 368(1)(c) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of a change to the information has been received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368B(1)(a) the lodged name and particulars are treated as those of the foreign company's directors` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company lodged the name and particulars of one or more directors under section 368(1)(c) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` AND (NOT `a notification of a change to the information has been received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a foreign company ... (a) has lodged the name and particulars of one or more directors ... are to be treated as the name and particulars of the company's director or directors ... until a notification of any change to the information is received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)" (an "if" gate and an "until" bar: marginal reading (a))

-- src:23912 | (b) has lodged the name and particulars of one or more agents
-- src:23913 | with the Registrar as an agent or agents (as the case may
-- src:23914 | be) of the foreign company under section 368(1)(e) in force
-- src:23915 | immediately prior to that date, the name and particulars of
-- src:23920 | the agent or agents (as the case may be) are to be treated as
-- src:23921 | the name and particulars of the company’s authorised
-- src:23922 | representative or representatives (as the case may be) until
-- src:23923 | a notification of any change to the information is received
-- src:23924 | by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca).
@ref s 368B(1)(b) (src:23912-23924)
GIVEN `the foreign company lodged the name and particulars of one or more agents under section 368(1)(e) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of a change to the information has been received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368B(1)(b) the lodged name and particulars of the agents are treated as those of the foreign company's authorised representatives` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company lodged the name and particulars of one or more agents under section 368(1)(e) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` AND (NOT `a notification of a change to the information has been received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) has lodged the name and particulars of one or more agents ... are to be treated as the name and particulars of the company's authorised representative or representatives ... until a notification of any change to the information is received by the Registrar under section 372(1)(ca)" (an "if" gate and an "until" bar: marginal reading (a))

-- src:23928 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:23930 | (a) the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of a
-- src:23931 | director under section 368(1)(c) in force immediately
-- src:23932 | before 3 January 2016 is to be treated as the director’s
-- src:23933 | residential address; and
@ref s 368B(2)(a) (src:23928-23933)
GIVEN `the address was lodged with the Registrar in respect of the director under section 368(1)(c) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368B(2)(a) the address lodged for a director is treated as the director's residential address` MEANS
    IF `the address was lodged with the Registrar in respect of the director under section 368(1)(c) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of a director under section 368(1)(c) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 is to be treated as the director's residential address" says nothing of another address

-- src:23935 | (b) the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of an agent
-- src:23936 | under section 368(1)(e) in force immediately before
-- src:23937 | 3 January 2016 is to be treated as the agent’s residential
-- src:23938 | address in the agent’s capacity as an authorised
-- src:23939 | representative of the foreign company.
@ref s 368B(2)(b) (src:23935-23939)
GIVEN `the address was lodged with the Registrar in respect of the agent under section 368(1)(e) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368B(2)(b) the address lodged for an agent is treated as the agent's residential address as authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the address was lodged with the Registrar in respect of the agent under section 368(1)(e) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of an agent under section 368(1)(e) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 is to be treated as the agent's residential address" says nothing of another address

§ `Section 369: refusal to register a foreign company`

-- src:23945 | Power to refuse registration of a foreign company in certain
-- src:23946 | circumstances
-- src:23948 | 369.—(1) Despite anything in this Act or any rule of law, the
-- src:23949 | Registrar must refuse to register a company under this Division if the
-- src:23950 | Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is being used or is
-- src:23951 | likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial
-- src:23952 | to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore or it would be
-- src:23953 | contrary to the national security or interest for the foreign company to
-- src:23954 | be registered.
@ref s 369(1) (src:23945-23954)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is being used or is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the foreign company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is being used or is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the foreign company to be registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must refuse to register a company under this Division if the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is being used or is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose ... or it would be contrary to the national security or interest" (a duty gated by "if": fork F-D1)

-- (2) "may, within 30 days of the date of the decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- src:23958 | (2) A foreign company aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar
-- src:23959 | under subsection (1) may, within 30 days of the date of the decision,
-- src:23960 | appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 369(2) (src:23958-23960)
GIVEN `the foreign company is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(2) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    IF NOT `the foreign company is aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign company aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (1)" names who may appeal, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the Registrar's decision` `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days of the date of the decision, appeal to the Minister" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 30 days of" is counted as "not later than 30 days after": fork F-P1)

@ref s 369(2) (src:23958-23960)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369(2) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appeal to the Minister whose decision is final" speaks only of an appeal under this subsection

§ `Section 370: the registered office and the authorised representatives`

DECLARE `s 370 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 370(1) keep a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public`
    `s 370(4) lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative`
    `s 370(6)(a) appoint another authorised representative`
    `s 370(7) appoint another authorised representative after the death of the sole authorised representative`

-- src:23962 | As to registered office and authorised representatives of
-- src:23963 | foreign companies
-- src:23965 | 370.—(1) A foreign company must have a registered office in
-- src:23966 | Singapore to which all communications and notices may be
-- src:23971 | addressed and which must be open and accessible to the public for not
-- src:23972 | less than 5 hours between the hours of 9 a.m. and 5 p.m. each business
-- src:23973 | day.
@ref s 370(1) (src:23962-23973)
GIVEN `the foreign company has a registered office in Singapore to which all communications and notices may be addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m. for which the registered office is open and accessible to the public on the business day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(1) the registered office meets the subsection on the business day` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has a registered office in Singapore to which all communications and notices may be addressed` AND `the number of hours between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m. for which the registered office is open and accessible to the public on the business day` AT LEAST 5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A foreign company must have a registered office in Singapore ... which must be open and accessible to the public for not less than 5 hours between the hours of 9 a.m. and 5 p.m. each business day" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

@ref s 370(1) (src:23965-23973)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 370 act`
`s 370(1) the foreign company must have a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 370(1) keep a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 370(1) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:23977 | (2) An authorised representative, until he or she ceases to be such in
-- src:23978 | accordance with subsection (5) —
-- src:23980 | (a) continues to be the authorised representative of the
-- src:23981 | company;
-- src:23983 | (b) is answerable for the doing of all such acts, matters and
-- src:23984 | things, as are required to be done by the company under
-- src:23985 | this Act; and
-- src:23987 | (c) shall be personally liable to all penalties imposed on the
-- src:23988 | company for any contravention of any of the provisions of
-- src:23989 | this Act unless he or she satisfies the court hearing the
-- src:23990 | matter that he or she should be not so liable.
@ref s 370(2) (src:23977-23990)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(2)(a) the person continues to be the authorised representative of the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorised representative, until he or she ceases to be such in accordance with subsection (5) — (a) continues to be the authorised representative of the company" ("until": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 370(2) (src:23977-23985)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(2)(b) the person is answerable for the acts, matters and things the foreign company must do under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorised representative, until he or she ceases to be such in accordance with subsection (5) — ... (b) is answerable for the doing of all such acts, matters and things, as are required to be done by the company under this Act" ("until": marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 370(2) (src:23977-23990)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has satisfied the court hearing the matter that he or she should not be so liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(2)(c) the person is personally liable to the penalties imposed on the foreign company for a contravention of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be an authorised representative in accordance with subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An authorised representative, until he or she ceases to be such in accordance with subsection (5) — ... (c) shall be personally liable to all penalties imposed on the company for any contravention" ("until": marginal reading (a); the text does not say who bears a penalty for a contravention made while the person was the representative and the notice has since taken effect: fork F-U2)
    ELSE (IF `the person has satisfied the court hearing the matter that he or she should not be so liable`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she satisfies the court hearing the matter that he or she should be not so liable"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:23994 | (3) A foreign company or its authorised representative may lodge
-- src:23995 | with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form stating that the
-- src:23996 | authorised representative has ceased to be the authorised
-- src:23997 | representative or will cease to be the authorised representative on a
-- src:23998 | date specified in the notice.
@ref s 370(3) (src:23994-23998)
GIVEN `the person is the foreign company or its authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(3) the person may lodge a notice that the authorised representative has ceased or will cease` MEANS
    IF `the person is the foreign company or its authorised representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A foreign company or its authorised representative may lodge with the Registrar a notice" names who may, without "only"

-- src:24000 | (4) On the appointment of a new authorised representative, the
-- src:24001 | company must lodge a notice mentioned in section 368(1)(e) and a
-- src:24002 | consent statement in respect of the new authorised representative
-- src:24003 | with the Registrar.
@ref s 370(4) (src:24000-24003)
GIVEN `a new authorised representative has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged the notice mentioned in section 368(1)(e) in respect of the new authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has lodged a consent statement in respect of the new authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(4) the foreign company has lodged the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` MEANS
    IF NOT `a new authorised representative has been appointed`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the appointment of a new authorised representative, the company must lodge ..." speaks only of an appointment
    ELSE (IF `the foreign company has lodged the notice mentioned in section 368(1)(e) in respect of the new authorised representative` AND `the foreign company has lodged a consent statement in respect of the new authorised representative`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must lodge a notice mentioned in section 368(1)(e) and a consent statement in respect of the new authorised representative with the Registrar" (a duty not met)

@ref s 370(4) (src:24000-24003)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 370 act`
`s 370(4) the foreign company must lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 370(4) lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 370(4) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (5) the day the authorised representative ceases: 21 days after lodgment, or the day the consent statement for another is lodged, whichever is the earlier,
-- but the date the notice states if that is later than the expiration of the 21 days. A sole authorised representative is the case of (6)(b), not of (5).
-- src:24007 | (5) Subject to subsections (6) and (7), the authorised representative
-- src:24008 | in respect of whom the notice under subsection (3) has been lodged
-- src:24009 | ceases to be an authorised representative on the expiration of a period
-- src:24010 | of 21 days after the date of lodgment of the notice or on the date on
-- src:24011 | which the consent statement in respect of another authorised
-- src:24012 | representative is lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1)(f),
-- src:24013 | whichever is the earlier, but if the notice states a date on which the
-- src:24014 | firstmentioned authorised representative is to so cease and the date is
-- src:24015 | later than the expiration of that period, on that date.
@ref s 370(5) (src:24007-24015)
GIVEN `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice under subsection (3) was lodged` IS A DATE
      `a consent statement in respect of another authorised representative has been lodged under section 368(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that consent statement was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the notice states a date on which the authorised representative is to cease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice states` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsections (6) and (7)": the sole authorised representative's case is s 370(6)(b)
    ELSE (IF `the notice states a date on which the authorised representative is to cease` AND `the date the notice states` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice under subsection (3) was lodged` 21 Days
          THEN JUST `the date the notice states`
          ELSE (IF `a consent statement in respect of another authorised representative has been lodged under section 368(1)(f)` AND `the day that consent statement was lodged` LESS THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice under subsection (3) was lodged` 21 Days
                THEN JUST `the day that consent statement was lodged`
                ELSE JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice under subsection (3) was lodged` 21 Days)))

-- src:24022 | (6) Where the authorised representative in respect of whom the
-- src:24023 | notice under subsection (3) has been lodged is the sole authorised
-- src:24024 | representative of a foreign company —
-- src:24026 | (a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised
-- src:24027 | representative; and
-- src:24029 | (b) the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised
-- src:24030 | representative of the foreign company on the date on which
-- src:24031 | the consent statement in respect of another authorised
-- src:24032 | representative is lodged under subsection (4).
@ref s 370(6) (src:24022-24032)
GIVEN `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the authorised representative in respect of whom the notice under subsection (3) has been lodged is the sole authorised representative of a foreign company — (a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative" (a duty gated by "Where": fork F-D1)

@ref s 370(6) (src:24029-24032)
GIVEN `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a consent statement in respect of another authorised representative has been lodged under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that consent statement was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 370(6)(b) the day the sole authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sole authorised representative of the foreign company` AND `a consent statement in respect of another authorised representative has been lodged under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST `the day that consent statement was lodged`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative of the foreign company on the date on which the consent statement in respect of another authorised representative is lodged under subsection (4)": until it is lodged the text names no date, and the 21 days of subsection (5) do not apply to a sole authorised representative

@ref s 370(6) (src:24022-24032)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 370 act`
`s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 370(6)(a) appoint another authorised representative`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 370(6)(a) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:24036 | (7) Where a foreign company’s sole authorised representative dies,
-- src:24037 | the company must, within 21 days after the death of the authorised
-- src:24038 | representative, appoint another authorised representative.
@ref s 370(7) (src:24036-24038)
GIVEN `the day the sole authorised representative died` IS A DATE
      `the day the foreign company appointed another authorised representative` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370(7) the foreign company appointed another authorised representative within 21 days after the death` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the sole authorised representative died` `the day the foreign company appointed another authorised representative` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, within 21 days after the death of the authorised representative, appoint another authorised representative" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a))

@ref s 370(7) (src:24036-24038)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 370 act`
`s 370(7) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative within 21 days after the death of the sole authorised representative` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 370(7) appoint another authorised representative after the death of the sole authorised representative`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company did not appoint another authorised representative within 21 days after the death of its sole authorised representative"

§ `Section 370A: the contact address of a director or authorised representative who is an individual (transition)`

-- "commencement date" in s 370A(6) is the date of commencement of section 47 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024.
-- That Act is not among the sources and the section's own text does not give the date, so it is a supplied fact: fork F-I1.
-- src:24082 | (6) In this section, “commencement date” means the date of
-- src:24083 | commencement of section 47 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory
-- src:24084 | Enhancements) Act 2024.
@ref s 370A(6) (src:24082-24084)
GIVEN `the date of commencement of section 47 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 370A(6) "commencement date" the commencement date` MEANS
    `the date of commencement of section 47 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`

-- src:24042 | Transitional provision for contact address of director or
-- src:24043 | authorised representative of foreign company
-- src:24045 | 370A.—(1) Where a director or authorised representative of a
-- src:24046 | foreign company (who is an individual) maintained an alternate
-- src:24047 | address with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the
-- src:24048 | commencement date, that address is taken to be the individual’s
-- src:24049 | contact address for the purposes of this Act, until notice of a change in
-- src:24050 | the individual’s contact address is lodged under any ACRA
-- src:24051 | administered Act on or after that date.
@ref s 370A(1) (src:24042-24051)
GIVEN `the individual maintained an alternate address with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370A(1) the alternate address is taken to be the individual's contact address` MEANS
    IF `the individual maintained an alternate address with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the commencement date` AND (NOT `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a director or authorised representative of a foreign company (who is an individual) maintained an alternate address with the Registrar ... immediately before the commencement date, that address is taken to be the individual's contact address ..., until notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged" (a "Where" gate and an "until" bar: marginal reading (a))

-- src:24053 | (2) Where a director or authorised representative of a foreign
-- src:24054 | company (who is an individual) did not maintain an alternate address
-- src:24055 | with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the
-- src:24056 | commencement date, the individual’s residential address is taken to
-- src:24057 | be the individual’s contact address for the purposes of this Act, until
-- src:24058 | notice of a change in the individual’s contact address is lodged under
-- src:24059 | any ACRA administered Act on or after that date.
@ref s 370A(2) (src:24053-24059)
GIVEN `the individual did not maintain an alternate address with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370A(2) the residential address is taken to be the individual's contact address` MEANS
    IF `the individual did not maintain an alternate address with the Registrar under this Act immediately before the commencement date` AND (NOT `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a director or authorised representative ... did not maintain an alternate address ..., the individual's residential address is taken to be the individual's contact address for the purposes of this Act, until notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged" (a "Where" gate and an "until" bar: marginal reading (a))

-- src:24061 | (3) An individual’s contact address mentioned in subsection (1) or
-- src:24062 | (2) is deemed, for the purposes of section 372(1)(ca), to be a
-- src:24063 | particular lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1).
@ref s 370A(3) (src:24061-24063)
GIVEN `the address is an individual's contact address mentioned in subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370A(3) the contact address is deemed to be a particular lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1) for section 372(1)(ca)` MEANS
    IF `the address is an individual's contact address mentioned in subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An individual's contact address mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) is deemed ..." speaks only of those addresses

-- src:24065 | (4) Subsection (5) applies to a notice or information required to be
-- src:24066 | lodged or given under section 368(1)(d) or (e), 368A(1), (2)(a), (3) or
-- src:24071 | (4) or 370(4) (as the case may be), relating to a director or authorised
-- src:24072 | representative of a foreign company appointed before the
-- src:24073 | commencement date.
-- src:24075 | (5) Where the notice or information mentioned in subsection (4) is
-- src:24076 | lodged or given on or after the commencement date, the notice or
-- src:24077 | information must provide the information required under section 368
-- src:24078 | as in force when the notice or information is lodged or given, despite
-- src:24079 | the director or authorised representative having been appointed
-- src:24080 | before the commencement date.
@ref s 370A(4), (5) (src:24065-24080)
GIVEN `the notice or information is one required to be lodged or given under section 368(1)(d) or (e), 368A(1), (2)(a), (3) or (4) or 370(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to a director or authorised representative appointed before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is lodged or given on or after the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 370A(5) the notice or information must provide the information required under section 368 as in force when it is lodged or given` MEANS
    IF `the notice or information is one required to be lodged or given under section 368(1)(d) or (e), 368A(1), (2)(a), (3) or (4) or 370(4)` AND `it relates to a director or authorised representative appointed before the commencement date` AND `it is lodged or given on or after the commencement date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the notice or information mentioned in subsection (4) is lodged or given on or after the commencement date, the notice or information must provide the information required under section 368 as in force when the notice or information is lodged or given" (a duty gated by "Where": fork F-D1)

§ `Section 371: the Registrar's notice and certificate of registration`

-- src:24088 | Transitory provisions
-- src:24090 | 371.—(1) On the registration of a foreign company under this
-- src:24091 | Division, the Registrar must issue a notice in the prescribed form and
-- src:24092 | the notice is prima facie evidence in all courts of the particulars
-- src:24093 | mentioned in the notice.
@ref s 371(1) (src:24088-24093)
GIVEN `the Registrar issued the notice in the prescribed form on the registration of the foreign company under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particular is mentioned in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(1) the notice is prima facie evidence of the particular in all courts` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar issued the notice in the prescribed form on the registration of the foreign company under this Division` AND `the particular is mentioned in the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the notice is prima facie evidence in all courts of the particulars mentioned in the notice" says nothing of a particular the notice does not mention

-- src:24095 | (2) Upon the application of the foreign company that has been duly
-- src:24096 | registered and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue
-- src:24097 | to the foreign company a certificate confirming the particulars
-- src:24098 | mentioned in the notice, and the certificate is prima facie evidence in
-- src:24099 | all courts of those particulars.
@ref s 371(2) (src:24095-24099)
GIVEN `the foreign company has been duly registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company has paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(2) the Registrar must issue the foreign company a certificate confirming the particulars` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company has been duly registered` AND `the foreign company has applied for the certificate` AND `the foreign company has paid the prescribed fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of the foreign company that has been duly registered and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the foreign company a certificate" (a duty gated by "Upon": fork F-D1)

@ref s 371(2) (src:24097-24099)
GIVEN `the Registrar issued the certificate confirming the particulars mentioned in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particular is mentioned in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 371(2) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the particular in all courts` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar issued the certificate confirming the particulars mentioned in the notice` AND `the particular is mentioned in the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the certificate is prima facie evidence in all courts of those particulars" says nothing of a particular the notice does not mention
